{"name":"Cyan Blue","hex":"#14a3c7","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cyan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An additive secondary colour midway between green and blue, evoked by wavelengths between ~490 and ~520 nm."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the colour cyan."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cyan"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cyan","blocks":[{"text":"Cyan is the color between blue and green on the visible spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a predominant wavelength between 490 and 520 nm, between the wavelengths of green and blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Nympheas_71293_3.jpg/330px-Nympheas_71293_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyan"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5